Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Kazuhiro Ohnishi
Title: Unilateral Decisions to Hire Managers in Markets with Capitalist and Labor-Managed Firms
Abstract: This paper examines the equilibrium outcomes of firms’ decision games to hire managers when there is a capitalist firm competing against a labor-managed firm. The paper shows that if only the capitalist firm hires a manager, then the equilibrium coincides with the solution when neither firm hires a manager. In addition, the paper shows that if only the labor-managed firm hires a manager, then at equilibrium the capitalist firm’s output and the market price are lower than when neither firm hires a manager.
Keywords: Capitalist firm,labor-managed firm,managerial delegation,mixed duopoly,Cournot model
Journal: International Journal of Management, Accounting and Economics
Pages: 190-196
Volume: 5
Issue: 4
Year: 2018
DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.17557451
